From 5db378613cfddf8902a11fbe73251a8275cdd116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:27:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gui tests: the nav lists expect the new masking tab (#3498)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

e698a688 moved what masking did out of Settings › Privacy into a page
of its own and gave it a nav tab: data-view="masking", between Usage
and Plugins, shown while the redact built-in is on (on by default, and
on in these tests' fixtures). The tests kept the old lists, so
builtins.test.cjs was red in both engines on main (#3498), and
sidebar.test.cjs (12 of 16) and gateway-mode.test.cjs (2 of 6) were
red for the same reason - found by running them; neither reported.

The lists now expect masking where the nav puts it. The assertions
stay exact deepEquals; nothing softened. page-width, view-no-sideways
and mobile-web keep page lists too, but only to visit each page - no
exact-list assertion, nothing red, nothing changed there.

Run: NODE_PATH=<npx playwright 1.57.0> node --test <spec>, chromium
and webkit: builtins 4 of 4, sidebar 16 of 16, gateway-mode 6 of 6;
reverting the lists alone puts every failure back (builtins fails at
the same "Sessions' and Library's tabs gone" assertion).

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
